{!-- the address shows with no prefix; the dropdown copies it in the form each kind of server searches for. Old markup, when the address itself was the one copy target with its `&`/`+` prefix:
<span
  data-role="group-address"
  phx-hook="Copy"
  id={"#{@id_prefix}-#{id(@group)}"}
  data-clipboard-text={@address}
  title={l("Click to copy the address")}
  class={@class, "cursor-copy [overflow-wrap:anywhere]"}
>
  {#case String.split(@address, "@", parts: 2)}
    {#match [handle, host]}
      {handle}<wbr>@{host}
    {#match _}
      {@address}
  {/case}
</span>
--}
{!-- `no_flip`: always below the address, since flipped up the panel went under the sticky page header. `strategy="fixed"`: placed against the viewport, so the hero's overflow clipping doesn't hide the panel below the address. `!w-max` on the panel: `.dropdown-panel` is a fixed 16rem, narrower than a long address, which then overflowed the panel and pushed its copy icon outside; it is as wide as the longest address instead, never wider than the screen --}
<Dropdown
  id={"#{@id_prefix}-#{id(@group)}"}
  position="bottom-start"
  no_flip
  strategy="fixed"
  close_on_select
  wrapper_class={@class}
  trigger_class="inline-flex items-start gap-1.5 text-left cursor-pointer"
  panel_class="text-base-content !w-max max-w-[calc(100vw-2rem)]"
  label={l("Copy the address")}
  trigger_opts={[
    "phx-hook": "Copy",
    "data-role": "group-address-trigger",
    "data-clipboard-text": @shown_address
  ]}
>
  <:trigger>
    <span data-role="group-address" class="[overflow-wrap:anywhere]">
      {!-- a line break, when one is needed, goes before the host rather than mid-word --}
      {#case String.split(@shown_address, "@", parts: 2)}
        {#match [handle, host]}
          {handle}<wbr>@{host}
        {#match _}
          {@shown_address}
      {/case}
    </span>
    <span data-role="copy-icon" class="shrink-0 mt-0.5"><#Icon iconify="ph:copy-duotone" class="size-4" /></span>
    <span data-role="copied-icon" class="hidden shrink-0 mt-0.5 text-success"><#Icon iconify="ph:check-bold" class="size-4" /></span>
  </:trigger>
  <li class="menu-title" data-role="group-address-heading">{l("Copy address as")}</li>
  {!-- one row per form, the saved one first; a signed-in user's pick is also saved (the click goes to the live handler as well as to the `Copy` hook, which copies client-side); a guest's pick is only copied. The link row only copies, and shows a label rather than the URL (it is in the `title`). Before this, the rows showed only a prefix and a label (`!…` "Lemmy, PieFed, Mbin…", `@…` "Mastodon and others", the link icon and "Link") --}
  {!-- `w-full` on the row, `flex!` on its button and `ml-auto` on the icons: each row takes the panel's full width (the widest address sets it), so the copy icons line up at the right edge rather than right after each address. `flex!` because daisyUI's menu makes a row's child a grid whose columns fit their content, which put each icon right after its address --}
  <li :for={row <- @rows} class="w-full">
    <button
      type="button"
      phx-hook="Copy"
      phx-click={if @save? and row.form != "link", do: "Bonfire.UI.Groups:set_address_form"}
      phx-value-form={row.form}
      id={"#{@id_prefix}-#{id(@group)}-#{row.dom_suffix}"}
      data-role="group-address-copy"
      data-form={row.form}
      data-clipboard-text={row.value}
      title={row.value}
      class="flex! items-center gap-2 w-full text-sm text-base-content whitespace-nowrap"
    >
      {#if row.form == "link"}
        <span class="flex-1 text-left">{l("Link")}</span>
      {#else}
        <span class="flex-1 text-left [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">{row.value}</span>
      {/if}
      <span data-role="copy-icon" class="ml-auto shrink-0 text-muted"><#Icon iconify="ph:copy-duotone" class="size-4" /></span>
      <span data-role="copied-icon" class="hidden ml-auto shrink-0 text-success"><#Icon iconify="ph:check-bold" class="size-4" /></span>
    </button>
  </li>
</Dropdown>
